mal. Trying to bluff at this pot with zero draws carries a risk that isn\'t justified by the small pot size. Checking back allows you to see the river card for free, potentially improving to a pair or reaching a cheap showdown.\n\nReason:\nYou have a very weak hand with no immediate draws. Since you are leading the overall game and the opponent has checked to you, taking a free card (Checking) is the safest play to preserve your chip lead and minimize variance.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
